  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1016 AM MDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nMoisture continues to stream in from the south indicated by \nhigh dewpoints across the region as well as PWATs of 150 to 200%\nof normal. Weak shortwaves will be moving through the mean \nflow, from southwest to northeast, and work on this moisture \nbringing another round of convection to the area. H7 winds are \non the order of 5 to 10kts so with light steering flow, some of \nthe convection will be slow moving. Thus, flash flooding under \nand near the stronger showers and storms will be possible once \nagain. Burn scars and other susceptible terrain will be the\nbiggest concerns. Can't rule out some hail and gusty outflow\nwinds as well. Convection will die down overnight but not\ncompletely end as some showers, maybe a rumble of thunder, are\nstill showing up in the CAMs. Rinse and repeat for Friday though\nmoisture content does decrease some. In fact, forecast PWATs are\nprogged to continue dropping through the weekend. Having said\nthat, residual moisture will remain allowing some convection\nover the higher terrain though coverage will be less than seen\nrecently. This diurnally driven convection continues through\nmidweek. After that, more widespread precip looks possible as \nweak low pressure system drifts by to our north. Highs will \nremain at or below normal today and tomorrow before reaching \nmore normal values and above for the weekend and the beginning \nof next week.",
